          "path": "_m/9/y/p/z/memphis-wk/related-sibling-stax-museum-of-american-soul-m.jpg",
          "filename": "Stax Museum of American Soul Music marquee.jpg",
          "caption": "Stax Museum of American Soul Music — exterior marquee. \n\nA fabulous stop for any music lover. In the heart of Soulsville USA and located at the site of the original Stax Recording Studios.\nThe museum pays tribute to Stax legendary artist roster including unknowns who would become icons, cranking out a massive catalog of smash soul hits by the likes of Isaac Hayes, Otis Redding, the Staple Singers, Wilson Pickett, Luther Ingram, Albert King, the Bar-Kays, Booker T. &amp; the MG's, Johnnie Taylor, Rufus and Carla Thomas, and dozens of other non-Stax artists who contributed to the soul music landscape.\nThe Otis Redding tribute is incredible.",
          "alt": "Stax Museum of American Soul Music — exterior marquee. \n\nA fabulous stop for any music lover. In the heart of Soulsville USA and located at the site of the original Stax Recording Studios.\nThe museum pays tribute to Stax legendary artist roster including unknowns who would become icons, cranking out a massive catalog of smash soul hits by the likes of Isaac Hayes, Otis Redding, the Staple Singers, Wilson Pickett, Luther Ingram, Albert King, the Bar-Kays, Booker T. &amp; the MG's, Johnnie Taylor, Rufus and Carla Thomas, and dozens of other non-Stax artists who contributed to the soul music landscape.\nThe Otis Redding tribute is incredible.",
          "width": 2864,
          "height": 2144,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Avalon Frost",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stax_Museum_of_American_Soul_Music_marquee.jpg",
          "sourceType": "core",
          "sourceArticleId": "memphis-wk",
          "sourceGeohash4": "9ypz",
          "accessedAt": "2026-02-22T01:10:00.539Z",
